---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
import Section from "@bundu/ui/Section.astro";
---

<Shell
  title="Circles on the fediverse · Mukoko Circles"
  description="Every open Mukoko circle has a fediverse address. Look circles up from Mastodon and other ActivityPub apps."
  canonical="https://circles.mukoko.com/fediverse"
>
  <section class="gradient-showcase border-b border-border">
    <div class="container-narrow py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">Fediverse</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-h1 text-balance">Every open circle has an address</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-muted-foreground">
        The fediverse is the network of independent social apps that talk to
        each other over ActivityPub: Mastodon, Pixelfed, Lemmy and many more.
        Mukoko circles are part of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section>
    <div class="container-prose space-y-10 px-0">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">The address</h2>
        <p>
          A circle's address is its name, then <span class="handle"
            >@circles.mukoko.com</span
          >. The Harare Runners circle, for example, would be:
        </p>
        <p class="card p-4 handle">@harare-runners@circles.mukoko.com</p>
        <p>
          Paste an address into the search box of your fediverse app to see the
          circle, its description and its public posts.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">What works today</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Looking a circle up by its address (WebFinger).</li>
          <li>
            Seeing the circle as a group, with its name, description and picture
            (an ActivityPub <code>Group</code> actor at
            <span class="handle">https://circles.mukoko.com/c/&lbrace;name&rbrace;</span>).
          </li>
          <li>
            Reading the posts its moderators have approved for the public (the
            outbox).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">What comes next</h2>
        <p>
          Following a circle from another server, and seeing its new posts in
          your timeline, needs signed deliveries between servers. That is the
          next phase. Until then, a circle's inbox says so plainly rather than
          pretending to accept a follow, and the way to join is the Mukoko app.
        </p>
        <p>
          The plan is tracked in the open, in
          <a class="link" href="https://github.com/mukoko-dev/mukoko-circles/issues/8"
            >mukoko-dev/mukoko-circles#8</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">For server admins</h2>
        <p>
          NodeInfo is at <a class="link" href="/.well-known/nodeinfo"
            >/.well-known/nodeinfo</a
          >. Private and secret circles are never federated, and posts are
          attributed to the circle, never to the person who wrote them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Shell>
